### ClearWood Furnitures — Prompt 9A: orders, payments and the Razorpay Route split
### VS Code REST Client. Runs top to bottom; @variables carry state forward.
###
### The story: a guest builds a cart, opens a checkout, places an order, pays with the MOCK driver,
### the webhook confirms it, the split pays two accounts, the ledger balances, replaying the
### webhook changes nothing, and a failed payment gives back every hold.
###
### Run the API with PAYMENT_DRIVER=mock. No network and no Razorpay account are needed.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1
@email = aarav.mehta@example.com
@password = CustomerDemo@2026

### ---------------------------------------------------- build a cart

### 1. Pick a product.
# @name product
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/banyan-live-edge-coffee-table

@productId = {{product.response.body.data.id}}
@variantId = {{product.response.body.data.variants.0.id}}

### 2. Add it. This mints the guest cart cookie (Prompt 8).
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "qty": 2 }

### 3. The cart, priced by the Prompt 6 engine.
# @name cart
GET {{api}}/cart

### ------------------------------------------------------- checkout

### 4. Open a checkout. Validates the cart with autoFix OFF and refuses on any BLOCKING issue,
### snapshots the address, checks serviceability, and remembers the hash of the quote.
# @name checkout
POST {{api}}/checkout/init
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contact": { "email": "guest@example.com", "phone": "919810000099" },
  "shippingAddress": {
    "fullName": "Guest Shopper",
    "phone": "919810000099",
    "line1": "9 Marine Drive",
    "city": "Mumbai",
    "state": "Maharashtra",
    "stateCode": "MH",
    "pincode": "400001"
  },
  "sameAsShipping": true
}

@sessionId = {{checkout.response.body.data.id}}

### 5. Read it back. `priceChanged` is false while the quote still matches.
GET {{api}}/checkout/{{sessionId}}

### 6. L1 — a body carrying an amount is REFUSED (422), not quietly ignored.
POST {{api}}/checkout/{{sessionId}}/place
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentProvider": "RAZORPAY", "amountPaise": 1, "grandTotalPaise": 1 }

### 7. Place it properly. The order, its items, its address snapshots, its stock reservations and
### its split allocations are all written in one transaction; the provider order comes after.
# @name placed
POST {{api}}/checkout/{{sessionId}}/place
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-place-0001

{ "paymentProvider": "RAZORPAY" }

@orderId = {{placed.response.body.data.orderId}}
@orderNumber = {{placed.response.body.data.orderNumber}}
@providerOrderId = {{placed.response.body.data.providerOrderId}}

### 8. Replaying the same place with the same Idempotency-Key returns the SAME order.
POST {{api}}/checkout/{{sessionId}}/place
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-place-0001

{ "paymentProvider": "RAZORPAY" }

### -------------------------------------------------------- payment

### 9. Admin login — needed for the ledger and split views below.
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@clearwood.local", "password": "ChangeMe@12345" }

### 10. See the allocations that were written BEFORE any money moved.
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/split-preview

### 11. The mock provider signs with a real HMAC over `${order_id}|${payment_id}`, so the
### verification below runs the production code path. Paste the ids from the mock simulator —
### in tests `mock.simulateCheckout()` produces them; here, use the webhook route instead.

### 12. THE WEBHOOK IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH. Deliver a signed payment.captured and the order
### confirms entirely on its own, with no verify call at all.
### (Signature = HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body with the mock webhook secret. Generate it with:
###   node -e "const{createHmac}=require('crypto');const b=process.argv[1];console.log(createHmac('sha256','mock_webhook_secret_for_tests_only').update(b).digest('hex'))" '<body>')
POST {{api}}/webhooks/razorpay
Content-Type: application/json
X-Razorpay-Signature: PASTE_THE_HMAC_HERE

{
  "id": "evt_demo_0001",
  "event": "payment.captured",
  "payload": { "payment": { "entity": { "id": "pay_demo_0001", "order_id": "{{providerOrderId}}", "amount": 0, "status": "captured", "method": "upi" } } }
}

### 13. Deliver the SAME event again. It is recorded as DUPLICATE and changes nothing.
POST {{api}}/webhooks/razorpay
Content-Type: application/json
X-Razorpay-Signature: PASTE_THE_HMAC_HERE

{
  "id": "evt_demo_0001",
  "event": "payment.captured",
  "payload": { "payment": { "entity": { "id": "pay_demo_0001", "order_id": "{{providerOrderId}}", "amount": 0, "status": "captured", "method": "upi" } } }
}

### 14. An unsigned delivery is rejected outright and never stored as valid.
POST {{api}}/webhooks/razorpay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "evt_unsigned", "event": "payment.captured", "payload": {} }

### 15. The browser's optimistic path, for comparison. Idempotent: if the webhook already
### confirmed the order this answers happily with `alreadyConfirmed: true`.
POST {{api}}/checkout/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "razorpay_order_id": "{{providerOrderId}}",
  "razorpay_payment_id": "pay_demo_0001",
  "razorpay_signature": "PASTE_THE_PAYMENT_HMAC_HERE"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------ the order

### 16. The order, rendered from its FROZEN snapshot — never re-quoted.
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}

### 17. Does the money balance? Every check must be ok.
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/ledger-check

### 18. Guest tracking: order number plus the contact on the order. Nothing sensitive comes back.
POST {{api}}/orders/track
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderNumber": "{{orderNumber}}", "email": "guest@example.com" }

### 19. A wrong contact answers the same 404 as a number that never existed.
POST {{api}}/orders/track
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderNumber": "{{orderNumber}}", "email": "not.this.person@example.com" }

### ------------------------------------------------------- the split

### 20. THE CANONICAL CASE. ₹6,000 splits to PRIMARY ₹5,000 + PARTNER_A ₹1,000, exactly.
POST {{api}}/admin/payments/split-simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amountPaise": 600000 }

### 21. The rules that produced it — data, not code.
GET {{api}}/admin/payments/split-rules

### 22. And the accounts they pay.
GET {{api}}/admin/payments/split-accounts

### 23. Retry only the FAILED payout legs. A successful transfer is never touched.
POST {{api}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/retry-transfers

### 24. Every stored provider event, with its status.
GET {{api}}/admin/webhooks?limit=20

### 25. Replay one from the admin. Idempotent by construction.
POST {{api}}/admin/webhooks/REPLACE_WITH_EVENT_ID/replay

### 26. Payment settings.
GET {{api}}/admin/payments/settings

### ----------------------------------------------- a failed payment

### 27. Build a second cart.
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "qty": 1 }

### 28. Open a checkout for it.
# @name failing
POST {{api}}/checkout/init
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contact": { "email": "guest@example.com" },
  "shippingAddress": {
    "fullName": "Guest Shopper",
    "phone": "919810000099",
    "line1": "9 Marine Drive",
    "city": "Mumbai",
    "state": "Maharashtra",
    "stateCode": "MH",
    "pincode": "400001"
  },
  "sameAsShipping": true
}

@failingSession = {{failing.response.body.data.id}}

### 29. Place it — stock and the coupon slot are now HELD.
# @name failingOrder
POST {{api}}/checkout/{{failingSession}}/place
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentProvider": "RAZORPAY" }

### 30. Abandon it. Every hold goes back: the reservation is RELEASED, the coupon slot returns,
### and the order lands in PAYMENT_FAILED. Nothing is stranded.
POST {{api}}/checkout/{{failingSession}}/abandon

### 31. Confirm it: the reservations on this order are all RELEASED.
GET {{api}}/admin/orders/{{failingOrder.response.body.data.orderId}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------- COD

### 32. Cash on delivery confirms with no provider call and creates no transfers.
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "qty": 1 }

### 33.
# @name codCheckout
POST {{api}}/checkout/init
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contact": { "email": "guest@example.com" },
  "shippingAddress": {
    "fullName": "Guest Shopper",
    "phone": "919810000099",
    "line1": "9 Marine Drive",
    "city": "Mumbai",
    "state": "Maharashtra",
    "stateCode": "MH",
    "pincode": "400001"
  },
  "sameAsShipping": true
}

### 34.
POST {{api}}/checkout/{{codCheckout.response.body.data.id}}/place
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentProvider": "COD" }

### ------------------------------------------------- customer orders

### 35. Sign in and read your own orders. Somebody else's order number answers 404, not 403.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 36.
GET {{api}}/me/orders

### 37.
GET {{api}}/me/orders/{{orderNumber}}

### 38.
GET {{api}}/me/orders/{{orderNumber}}/timeline

### 39. Cancel it. Holds are released and a Refund row is created in REQUESTED — executing that
### refund is Prompt 9B.
POST {{api}}/me/orders/{{orderNumber}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "CUSTOMER_REQUEST", "note": "changed my mind" }

### ----------------------------------------------------- the sweep

### 40. Reconciliation: asks the provider for the truth before releasing anything, then reports
### captured-without-transfers, allocation mismatches and orphan reservations.
POST {{api}}/admin/orders/reconcile
Content-Type: application/json

{ "olderThanMinutes": 0, "limit": 50 }
